      "text_raw": "Active entities: U.S., National Review, CBC News, Andrew Yang. Topic: presidential candidate Andrew Yang became his The uniformity of these memes is encouraged by their rapid imitation among the genre 's hyperactive online subculture , fueled by affective contagion[90 ] Pitchfork contributor Jonny Coleman defined vaporwave as residing in \" the uncanny genre valley \" that lies \" between a real genre that sounds fake and a fake genre that could be real . \"[52 ] Also from Pitchfork , Patrick St. Michel calls vaporwave a \" niche corner of Internet music populated by Westerners goofing around with Japanese music , samples , and language\".[91 ] Vice writer Rob Arcand commented that the \" rapid proliferation of subgenres has itself become part of the \" vaporwave \" punchline , gesturing at the absurdity of the genre itself even as it sees artists using it as a springboard for innovation . \"[23 ] Speaking about the \" supposedly subversive or parodic elements \" of vaporwave in 2018 , cultural critic Simon Reynolds said that the genre had been made redundant , in some respects , by modern trap music and mainstream hip hop . He opined : \" What could be more insane or morbid than the subjectivity in a Drake record or a Kanye song ? The black Rap n B mainstream is further out sonically and attitudinally than anything the white Internet-Bohemia has come up with . Their role is redundant . Rap and R & B ... is already the Simulacrum , is already decadence . \"[92 ] Upcoming entities: Monkees, Mike Nesmith, Vaporwave. Next focus: that reported Monkees",
